From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:26:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 52/72] deepseek: TF_DSV41_IDX_SPLIT exactness oracle over the
 emitted programs

A host model of the selection kernels and glue (scores with ties, int64
score/position keys, top-k, stream splits and merge, candidate blocks,
reindex) runs the replicated program and both split ranks' programs from the
same inputs, the ranks in lockstep through glueCut / Cut.plan. Every row's
selection, each rank's own candidates and every row's scanned key range must
match. Cases cross a stream-split boundary, ragged parts and many row blocks a
rank; planted NK, block position, nsplit, merge-row and cut defects must fail.
